## Why This Is Asked
High-scale streaming systems require robust end-to-end validation that goes beyond unit testing. Organizations need assurance that their pipelines handle schema evolution, late data, and data drift while maintaining consistency between staging and production environments.

## Key Concepts
- End-to-end data validation across landing areas and warehouse
- Idempotent MERGE/upsert semantics ensuring data consistency
- Late data and backfill handling with drift detection mechanisms
- Traffic simulation and CI-backed regression testing
- Schema evolution compatibility validation
- Data reconciliation and consistency checks

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-test: hash payload for idempotency validation
const crypto = require('crypto');
function hashPayload(payload) {
  return crypto.createHash('sha256')
    .update(JSON.stringify(payload))
    .digest('hex');
}

// Validate idempotent upserts by comparing hash signatures
```

## Why This Is Asked
Real-time pipelines present subtle consistency and resilience challenges that unit tests alone cannot catch. Interviewers want to see that you understand end-to-end testing across distributed systems, including CI/CD integration.

## Key Concepts
- Exactly-once semantics via transactional sinks and checkpointing
- Stateful stream processing and its failure modes
- Backward/forward schema evolution to prevent consumer breakage
- Backpressure handling, failure recovery, and replay safety
- Observability within CI/CD pipelines

## Code Example
```javascript
// Verify exactly-once processing with idempotent writes
const result = await warehouse.query(`
  SELECT event_id, COUNT(*) as score_count
  FROM risk_scores
  GROUP BY event_id
  HAVING COUNT(*) > 1
`);
assert(result.length === 0, 'Duplicate events detected');

// Validate replay safety after simulated outage
await kafka.broker.crash({ node: 3 });
await flink.restartFromCheckpoint();
const postRecoveryScores = await warehouse.fetchLatestScores();
assert(postRecoveryScores.length === expectedCount);
```

